WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.040
A misty churchyard.

2
00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:05.480
A paved road runs from
it to a distant city.

3
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:09.360
A small boy sets off,
growing taller as he walks.

4
00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:11.650
Three milestones pass.

5
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:17.820
And the book itself announces: "This is the
end of the first stage of Pip’s expectations."

6
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:21.040
A life story, cut into three stages.

7
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.000
Why would Dickens do that?

8
00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:25.940
In this mission, you'll
meet the bildungsroman:

9
00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:30.300
a novel about growing up, told
by an older Pip looking back.

10
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.960
You'll see how it first came out: weekly,

11
00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.260
in Dickens's own magazine, 36 instalments,

12
00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:41.210
from 1 December 1860 to 3 August 1861.

13
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:45.870
And you'll find where the narrator
himself draws a line under each stage.

14
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:51.080
Your mission: work out why Dickens
splits Pip's life into three stages.
